  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ayub Khalid Khatri And Anr vs State Of Maharashtra on 8 March, 2024 Author: N. J. Jamadar Bench: N. J. Jamadar 901-Aba349-2024.Doc Santosh In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 349 Of 2024 Ayub Khalid Khatri and anr. ...Applicants Versus State of Maharashtra ...Respondent Mr. Rizwan Merchant, a/w Sagar Shete and Sultan Khan, for the Applicant. Ms. Ranjana Humane, App for the State/Respondent. Coram: N. J. Jamadar, J. Dated: 8th March, 2024 Pc:- 1.",
    "facts": "2. This is an application for pre-arrest bail in connection with CR No.112 of 2023, registered with Igatpuri Police Station, Nashik Rural, for the offences punishable under Sections 328, 272, 273, 420, 188, 465, 468, 471 read with 34 of Indian Penal Code, 1860 (\"the Penal Code\") and Sections 23(2)(i), 26(2)(ii), 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(e), 30(2)(a) and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. an order dated 4th September, 2023, this Court has granted ad-interim relief to the co-accused. This Court was persuaded to grant ad- interim relief to the co-accused as the applicability of provisions of Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860 (\"the Penal Code\") is debatable and the issue is pending before the Supreme Court. In identical matters, this Court has granted interim protection to the persons, who have been arraigned for the offence punishable under Section 328 of the Penal Code.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
